From: Project Luma <luma@project-luma.org>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 20:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/a810: use the Gen8.3 GMU AHB fence range

Fairphone's Android 16 Qualcomm graphics driver programs the Gen8.3 GMU AHB
fence lower bound to 0x8a0. The Milos DRM driver instead applies the generic
A8xx lower bound of 0x8c0 to A810.

The FP6 timeout diagnostic established that the GMU cold-boots with correct
core and hub clocks and begins executing far enough to advance its retained
log pointer, but never sets CM3_FW_INIT_RESULT. Match the authoritative Gen8.3
fence range for A810 while leaving every other A8xx GPU unchanged.

This is a one-variable behavior test. It must remain RAM-only until a bounded
FP6 workload completes without a GMU timeout, GPU/DPU hangcheck, or recovery
failure.

---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
index 654fd304a..3e7477cd4 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
@@ -1009,7 +1009,7 @@ static int a6xx_gmu_fw_start(struct a6xx_gmu *gmu, unsigned int state)
 
 	if (adreno_is_a8xx(adreno_gpu)) {
 		fence_range_upper = 0x32;
-		fence_range_lower = 0x8c0;
+		fence_range_lower = adreno_is_a810(adreno_gpu) ? 0x8a0 : 0x8c0;
 	} else if (adreno_is_a7xx(adreno_gpu)) {
 		fence_range_upper = 0x32;
 		fence_range_lower = 0x8a0;
-- 
2.51.0
